From 7e25e5d4dc03a6133a08a6f8685b3c64f7d3224e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: manerger <filidog82@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:06:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] mb/asustek_computer/k53sc: Consolidate the EC access
 primitives

The drain, wait-for-IBF and write helpers had been copied into three
files as each stage grew a need for them: early_init.c for the Tjmax
handoff, smihandler.c for the ACPI mode SMI, and mainboard.c for the S3
resume path. Move them into ec.c, build it for bootblock, romstage,
ramstage and smm, and expose the three operations the board actually
performs through ec.h.

This also settles an inconsistency between the copies: early_init.c's
wait loop issued the I/O delay before testing the status bit, while the
other two tested first. Stock reads, tests, then delays, so the shared
version does that.

The derivation of the ACPI mode sequences now sits in ec.c beside the
command bytes rather than in a comment in the SMI handler.

No functional change intended. Tested on an ASUS K53SC with an
i7-3840QM: the machine boots, the volume keys work, and they still work
after a suspend and resume, which exercises the SMM and ramstage callers
respectively. The bootblock caller runs on every boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
